In my quest to ascend all character types Ranger was next.  This was, by 
far, my hardest ascention.  I made 3 major mistakes but somehow survived all 
of them.

It wasn't difficult due to the class so much, but an extremely stingy RNG. 
There was only one altar generated, besides Moloch's and the minetown, on 
dlv 4.  I had to hike all the way back to 4 every time I needed the altar. 
Other odd happenings - I never got teleport/control, potions were extremely 
rare, found 1 magic marker (wished for another), many other difficulties.

Rangers to me seem inherently difficult because a bow isn't a great main 
weapon, and you can't twoweapon.  I used Stormbringer most of the time, even 
though it cost me.

I used a lot of pets this time.  I started with a Minotaur and Skeleton.  I 
used them to wipe out all (but one) of the shopkeepers and pretty much all 
else.  Later I went with an arch-lich, which was my first near-critical 
mistake.  At one point I left him behind to go back for something I forgot, 
and when I returned of course he forgot about me.  By then he had nearly 300 
hit points and Stormbringer has no level drain against him.  An hour long 
battle ensued where I fought his monster storms and he cursed most of my 
stuff.  I knew not to use a Lich for a pet for just this reason, but I 
intended to abandon him in a side-quest somewhere.  I don't think I'll risk 
it again.

In Gehennom I used a set of purple worms, which make excellent pets until 
they eventually eat a green slime, that's how I lose most of them.

My second critical mistake was getting surrounded by an arch-lich, a bunch 
of nasties and no escape route.  The L summoned a 'c', which I killed and 
picked up without my gloves on.  Used an amulet of life saving here.

The end of the game was very difficult because I had very little holy water 
(ran out before the elemental plains), no scrolls of remove curse, and 
potions of healing were quite rare.  I got my hp up to 400 my scavenging all 
the healing potions I could and mixing.  I don't genocide so I lost my 
memory many times due to mind flayers, but with the Identify spell at 0% 
fail it wasn't a big deal.

I had no scrolls of gold detection, so I had to find the endgame portals the 
hard way.  The Astral plane was where I made my 3rd critical mistake.  My 
bag of holding got un-blessed, and rather than fight burdened I dropped it, 
intending to come back for it when I found my altar.  The bag had all my 
loot in it, about 130k gold and all my gems, plus some odd artifacts.  I 
took a few potions of full healing along, and found my altar with Pestilence 
in the middle.  When I killed all the major baddies, I started back for my 
loot, but then a bunch of monsters were summoned, along with an Archon.  The 
Archon blinded/stunned me, and while stunned I whacked my aligned High 
Priest with Stormbringer.  Surrounded by several priests, the High priest 
and the Archon my HP's were dropping quickly.  I drank one full-healing 
potion and tried to get away, but the Archon would stun me every other step. 
I was plainly not getting out alive.  Getting out the door into Pestilence's 
waiting arms, while stunned and without a blessed unicorn horn seemed like a 
bad idea.  I wobbled as best I could to the altar, and still surrounded and 
down to almost 50% hp, I just offered the amulet.  Leaving the loot behind 
cost me points, but I thought it'd be a shame to not ascend after fighting 
the terrible RNG the whole game.

During the endgame, a lot of stuff in my inventory vanished.  I lost some 
full healing potions and rings.  Where could they have gone?

So that's it for Rangers, and I don't think I'll play one again.  Not 
without the arrow-identifying patch I've read about, which might make them 
tolerable.

